# Build/bootstrap toolchain (P37-03 step 3).
#
# Why this file exists, measured rather than assumed: a fresh CPython 3.13 venv
# contains `pip 24.2` and NOTHING ELSE - ensurepip stopped shipping setuptools
# in 3.12. So on a clean machine:
#
#   pip install .                      -> build isolation downloads an UNLOCKED
#                                         setuptools from PyPI, straight past
#                                         every hash in requirements/*.txt
#   pip install --no-build-isolation . -> ModuleNotFoundError: setuptools
#
# Neither is acceptable, and "the venv usually has setuptools" is not true here.
# So the build toolchain is locked like everything else, installed first with
# --require-hashes, and the project is then built with --no-build-isolation so
# nothing is fetched outside the lock.
#
# Compiled by: python tools/compile_locks.py  (target: requirements/bootstrap.txt)
pip
setuptools
